+`fc-01M60N2X5ZXVR69E5NCGH8W7ZN` were already complete. Other experiments' apps
+were inventoried and left alone (`results/modal_apps_before.json`).
+
+The even split has **zero read errors in 24,576 reads**. Every eligible k from 1
+through 16 ties, so the registered rule selects **k = 1**. This satisfies the
+registered conflict-count definition of identification, but does **not** identify
+a physical address length. The odd split has 3 errors on 24,528 conflict reads:
+**q = 0.0001223092**, Wilson 95% [0.0000415963, 0.0003595803]. Its 48 no-conflict
+reads have no errors; all are at step zero. Thus there is almost no useful
+no-conflict control in the estimation data. Median / p10 margins are 16.25 / 13.75
+on conflicts and 14.125 / 11.925 off conflicts. These are output logit gaps, not
+raw attention scores.
+
+| Events | Tapes | Predicted exact | Recorded exact | Absolute gap |
+| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
+| 2,048 | 96 | 0.7785 | 0.8750 | 0.0965 |
+| 4,096 | 96 | 0.6060 | 0.6146 | 0.0086 |
+| 8,192 | 96 | 0.3672 | 0 | **0.3672** |
+| 12,000 | 80 | 0.2305 | 0 | **0.2305** |
+
+Mean first-error log score over 368 tapes is −5.7291 nats. Improvements over
+log dilution, inverse-t dilution, position-only, and the short-fit lognormal are
+respectively +0.2075, +1.7313, +0.2288, and +0.8869. All exceed the 0.05 bar;
+calibration fails the 0.15 bar at both longest lengths. With k = 1 almost every
+random-tape position conflicts, so this fit acts approximately as a constant
+hazard. Beating weak short-fit baselines does not establish a collision mechanism.
+
+Elevator, excluded from fitting and the pass pool, has exact rates 0.625, 0.125,
+0, 0 against the same predicted survivals. The deliberately post-hoc lognormal
+fit on the held-out outcomes scores −5.4848 nats on those same outcomes; it is
+neither an independent prediction nor a rescue of the claim.
+
+REGVM's four true transcripts were reconstructed read-only. There are
+507, 507, 508, and 506 conflicting first-symbol positions in their first 512
+steps; all four published failure positions (2,743, 4,193, 1,811, 2,533) also
+conflict. Because ambiguity is already nearly universal in the short window,
+this descriptive check does not explain when failure starts. Lag emits rewrite
+results rather than copying a separate input tape; no transfer of Savant's q is
+claimed. Symbol-level strings and newlines here are abstract tokens, not the
+REGVM model's tokenizer IDs.
+
+**Measurement limitations.** The registered estimator uses the first 512 run
+events of a 1,024-event question, and searches that entire question for conflicts.
+It therefore estimates from short *run prefixes*, not from contexts containing
+at most 512 total events as the brief literally requests. The existing probe
+summaries also average **state-query attention over all heads**, despite the
+estimator's `reading_heads_bin_0_256` label; the eight reading-head names alone
+do not make those mass summaries reading-head score statistics. No raw scores
+or values are recoverable from these summaries. These limitations further rule
+out claiming the surviving C2 result. Neither limitation is repaired by changing
+the registered fit after seeing its failures.
+
+### 4.1 Frozen prospective manifest (before any intervention forward)
+
+`results/intervention_manifest.json` contains the actual event tapes, token-ID
+hashes, realized conflicts, and every model's survival prediction; it binds the
+estimate by SHA-256. `results/intervention_plan.json` is the compact summary.
+All tapes fit at 8,192 (maximum 24,739 tokens), so no length substitution occurs.
+
+| Regime | Distinct tapes per length | Conflicts, short / long | Predicted survival, short / long |
+| --- | ---: | --- | --- |
+| Z | 16 | 0 / 0 | 1 / 1 |
+| H | 11 | 1,024–1,536 / 4,096–6,144 | 0.8482 / 0.5205 |
+| F | 12 paired | 1,535 or 2,046 / identical within each pair | 0.8037 / 0.8037 |
+
+At k = 1 the registered H draw sequence contains duplicates: five at each
+length. To honor §2.7's **distinct tapes** requirement, retain the first occurrence
+of each tape and do not draw replacements or change seeds. This makes H
+inconclusive under the pre-existing n ≥ 12 rule, whatever its observed rates.
+F generates only 12 distinct prefixes at k = 1 and meets its n ≥ 8 rule.
+The 78 distinct intervention tapes will still test the frozen prospective hazard
+and report all three contrasts. Repeated copies of a deterministic prompt are
+not independent examples.
+
+**Descriptive supplement, declared after the fit but before GPU measurements.**
+`hz_stats.py` will measure the eight pre-named heads on twelve fresh 256-event
+tapes (two per trained family, seed 7071), at read steps 16, 32, 64, 128, 255.
+It will save target/background scores, actual target value vectors, and the
+softmax-weighted background value mean (plus the unweighted mean for comparison).
+This fills a measurement gap with genuinely short tapes; these quantities will
+not enter the prediction, refit k/q, or count as independent confirmation.
+
+The GPU cap is recorded as $15 before any spawn. Prices were checked against
