+
+## 5. Short-tape score and value supplement
+
+**Unaudited, descriptive, collected after freezing the predictor.** The twelve
+256-event tapes produced 480 head/query observations (60 per head). The saved
+`short-stats/short_values.npz` contains the corresponding 128-dimensional target,
+softmax-weighted background, and unweighted-background vectors. All are finite;
+their norms and target-to-bath distances reproduce the JSON statistics.
+
+| Head | Target score | Background mean | Background SD | Target attention | Target value norm | Weighted bath norm | Target–bath distance |
+| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
+| L23.H4 | 23.15 | 6.74 | 4.38 | .702 | 11.37 | 7.69 | 9.70 |
+| L23.H5 | 16.88 | 4.98 | 3.34 | .341 | 11.37 | 5.87 | 9.64 |
+| L23.H30 | 15.34 | 3.68 | 3.31 | .273 | 10.66 | 4.69 | 8.55 |
+| L24.H5 | 18.19 | 4.53 | 3.85 | .342 | 15.07 | 9.38 | 14.35 |
+| L24.H13 | 14.46 | 3.50 | 3.32 | .246 | 11.19 | 6.81 | 9.29 |
+| L24.H20 | 25.28 | 6.44 | 4.95 | .891 | 17.10 | 10.40 | 16.63 |
+| L24.H22 | 37.33 | 9.32 | 7.37 | .971 | 17.10 | 11.28 | 17.49 |
+| L24.H23 | 33.28 | 7.55 | 6.63 | .976 | 17.10 | 10.83 | 16.54 |
+
+Entries average per-query measurements, including the per-query background SD;
+they are not moments of one pooled Gaussian. Background means every causally
+visible key except the current target event, including prompt, table, sink and
+run tokens. Scores are scaled, post-RoPE QK products; values precede output
+projection. The weighted and unweighted background means differ in normed
+distance by 4.55–8.85 across heads. A single Gaussian background assumption and
+an unweighted value bath are therefore not established by these measurements.
+No score-to-accuracy law, asymptotic horizon, or causal mediation claim follows
+from this table. It supplies the measurements missing from the existing records,
+without retroactively changing the registered experiment.
+
+## 6. Intervention outcome
+
+**Unaudited.** All 78 planned tapes were scored, with no missing records, changed
+tapes, replacement draws, refits, or length substitutions. The 256-event smoke
+is excluded. Every first-error record, error count, margin and argmax was checked
+against the downloaded per-token NPZ arrays.
+
+| Regime | Length | Failures / tapes | First read / first state | Frozen predicted failure |
+| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
+| Z | 2,048 | 2 / 16 | 0 / 2 | 0 |
+| Z | 8,192 | 1 / 16 | 0 / 1 | 0 |
+| H | 2,048 | 0 / 11 | 0 / 0 | .1518 |
+| H | 8,192 | 2 / 11 | 0 / 2 | .4795 |
+| F | 2,048 | 12 / 12 | 11 / 1 | .1963 |
+| F | 8,192 | 12 / 12 | 10 / 2 | .1963 |
+
+The collision gaps Δ_C are **−.1250** and **+.1193**. Length gaps Δ_L(Z),
+Δ_L(H), Δ_F are **−.0625, +.1818, 0**. The registered numerical reading is
+**mixed**, independently of H being below its distinct-tape floor. The causal
+test therefore does not pass, and is formally **inconclusive**, not evidence for
+the opposite universal claim that length alone causes failure.
+
+| Frozen model | Prospective mean log score | Collision minus this model |
+| --- | ---: | ---: |
+| Collision | −4.45727 | — |
+| Log dilution | −3.88656 | −.57071 |
+| Inverse-t dilution | −4.40702 | −.05025 |
+| Position-only | −3.85854 | −.59873 |
+| Short-fit lognormal | −4.14613 | −.31114 |
+
+The prospective test **fails against every alternative**. Zero-conflict first
+errors are state errors, so they refute this predictor of *any first run error*,
+not a claim that every read error requires a suffix conflict. There are no first
+read errors in Z or H. Of F's 24 first errors, 21 are reads: **19 at step 2,046**,
+exactly the first new tail symbol, and two earlier on long tapes (992 and 1,075).
+Three are state errors. Thus F's failure rate is saturated at both lengths;
+Δ_F = 0 is not persuasive evidence of length independence. Several pairs change
+first-error timing or kind despite equal conflict counts.
+
+The constructed regimes also change periodicity, symbol frequency and boundary
+novelty, and hold the literal table fixed. They are not random samples from a
+population or a surgical intervention on attention keys. Wilson bars in the
+machine-readable summary and figure are descriptive binomial intervals, not a
+causal confidence guarantee. With one frozen program, few distinct tapes and
+an inconclusive H cell, the evidence supports rejection of this registered
+constant-q model, not a general rejection of content-address interference.
+
+![Held-out calibration and intervention outcomes, unaudited](results/horizon.png)
+
+## 7. Consequence for the paper
+
+Do **not** add a predictive horizon law or "collisions, not decay" conclusion to
+the paper. C2's narrowed contribution has not been achieved. A suitable statement
+for the "where does it fail" section is:
+
+> On Savant r2's trained formats, a preregistered suffix-conflict hazard estimated
+> from early run prefixes beat four short-fit baselines in held-out log score,
+> but substantially overpredicted survival at 8k and 12k events. Constructed
+> tapes did not reproduce the required collision-versus-length contrasts, and
+> the frozen hazard lost to all four baselines prospectively. Sparse, clustered
+> short-context errors did not identify an effective address length or a stable
+> conflict sensitivity. These unaudited results do not support a quantitative
+> collision horizon for this executor.
+
+Boundary-sensitive errors and separate read/state hazards are possible follow-up
+hypotheses, explicitly **post-hoc**, not discoveries established by this test.
+The short-tape score/value measurements are descriptive evidence only. The
+birthday and lognormal calculations remain classical conditional models, as
+GATE §C2 requires. No new theorem, universal mechanism or fitted-curve rescue is
+claimed. No additional spend is needed to report this negative result.
+
