+`fc-01M60N2X5ZXVR69E5NCGH8W7ZN` were already complete. Other experiments' apps
+were inventoried and left alone (`results/modal_apps_before.json`).
+
+The even split has **zero read errors in 24,576 reads**. Every eligible k from 1
+through 16 ties, so the registered rule selects **k = 1**. This satisfies the
+registered conflict-count definition of identification, but does **not** identify
+a physical address length. The odd split has 3 errors on 24,528 conflict reads:
+**q = 0.0001223092**, Wilson 95% [0.0000415963, 0.0003595803]. Its 48 no-conflict
+reads have no errors; all are at step zero. Thus there is almost no useful
+no-conflict control in the estimation data. Median / p10 margins are 16.25 / 13.75
+on conflicts and 14.125 / 11.925 off conflicts. These are output logit gaps, not
+raw attention scores.
+
+All three short-window read errors occur in **one prose tape**, at steps
+207, 208, and 215. The latter two follow its first error under teacher forcing.
+The registered q estimator is a read-token error rate, not an empirical hazard
+conditioned on natural-rollout survival. Treating its Wilson interval as an
+independent-tape uncertainty estimate would be unjustified; within-tape errors
+and collisions are correlated.
+
+| Events | Tapes | Predicted exact | Recorded exact | Absolute gap |
+| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
+| 2,048 | 96 | 0.7785 | 0.8750 | 0.0965 |
+| 4,096 | 96 | 0.6060 | 0.6146 | 0.0086 |
+| 8,192 | 96 | 0.3672 | 0 | **0.3672** |
+| 12,000 | 80 | 0.2305 | 0 | **0.2305** |
+
+Mean first-error log score over 368 tapes is −5.7291 nats. Improvements over
+log dilution, inverse-t dilution, position-only, and the short-fit lognormal are
+respectively +0.2075, +1.7313, +0.2288, and +0.8869. All exceed the 0.05 bar;
+calibration fails the 0.15 bar at both longest lengths. With k = 1 almost every
+random-tape position conflicts, so this fit acts approximately as a constant
+hazard. Beating weak short-fit baselines does not establish a collision mechanism.
+
+Elevator, excluded from fitting and the pass pool, has exact rates 0.625, 0.125,
+0, 0 against the same predicted survivals. The deliberately post-hoc lognormal
+fit on the held-out outcomes scores −5.4848 nats on those same outcomes; it is
+neither an independent prediction nor a rescue of the claim.
+
+REGVM's four true transcripts were reconstructed read-only. There are
+507, 507, 508, and 506 conflicting first-symbol positions in their first 512
+steps; all four published failure positions (2,743, 4,193, 1,811, 2,533) also
+conflict. Because ambiguity is already nearly universal in the short window,
+this descriptive check does not explain when failure starts. Lag emits rewrite
+results rather than copying a separate input tape; no transfer of Savant's q is
+claimed. Symbol-level strings and newlines here are abstract tokens, not the
+REGVM model's tokenizer IDs.
+
+**Measurement limitations.** The registered estimator uses the first 512 run
+events of a 1,024-event question, and searches that entire question for conflicts.
+It therefore estimates from short *run prefixes*, not from contexts containing
+at most 512 total events as the brief literally requests. The existing probe
+summaries also average **state-query attention over all heads**, despite the
+estimator's `reading_heads_bin_0_256` label; the eight reading-head names alone
+do not make those mass summaries reading-head score statistics. No raw scores
+or values are recoverable from these summaries. These limitations further rule
+out claiming the surviving C2 result. Neither limitation is repaired by changing
+the registered fit after seeing its failures.
+
+### 4.1 Frozen prospective manifest (before any intervention forward)
+
+`results/intervention_manifest.json` contains the actual event tapes, token-ID
+hashes, realized conflicts, and every model's survival prediction; it binds the
+estimate by SHA-256. `results/intervention_plan.json` is the compact summary.
+All tapes fit at 8,192 (maximum 24,739 tokens), so no length substitution occurs.
+
+| Regime | Distinct tapes per length | Conflicts, short / long | Predicted survival, short / long |
+| --- | ---: | --- | --- |
+| Z | 16 | 0 / 0 | 1 / 1 |
+| H | 11 | 1,024–1,536 / 4,096–6,144 | 0.8482 / 0.5205 |
+| F | 12 paired | 1,535 or 2,046 / identical within each pair | 0.8037 / 0.8037 |
+
+At k = 1 the registered H draw sequence contains duplicates: five at each
+length. To honor §2.7's **distinct tapes** requirement, retain the first occurrence
+of each tape and do not draw replacements or change seeds. This makes H
+inconclusive under the pre-existing n ≥ 12 rule, whatever its observed rates.
+F generates only 12 distinct prefixes at k = 1 and meets its n ≥ 8 rule.
+The 78 distinct intervention tapes will still test the frozen prospective hazard
+and report all three contrasts. Repeated copies of a deterministic prompt are
+not independent examples.
+
+**Descriptive supplement, declared after the fit but before GPU measurements.**
+`hz_stats.py` will measure the eight pre-named heads on twelve fresh 256-event
+tapes (two per trained family, seed 7071), at read steps 16, 32, 64, 128, 255.
+It will save target/background scores, actual target value vectors, and the
+softmax-weighted background value mean (plus the unweighted mean for comparison).
+This fills a measurement gap with genuinely short tapes; these quantities will
+not enter the prediction, refit k/q, or count as independent confirmation.
+
+The GPU cap is recorded as $15 before any spawn. Prices were checked against
+[Modal's list prices](https://modal.com/pricing) on 29 October 2026. The ledger
+uses GPU + requested CPU/memory, wall time plus a 180-second startup allowance;
+this is an estimate, not an invoice. Jobs use an isolated HORIZON output volume,
+read-only PROMPTBOX adapter, bounded remote timeouts and nonblocking local polls.
+
+## 5. Short-tape score and value supplement
+
+**Unaudited, descriptive, collected after freezing the predictor.** The twelve
+256-event tapes produced 480 head/query observations (60 per head). The saved
+`short-stats/short_values.npz` contains the corresponding 128-dimensional target,
+softmax-weighted background, and unweighted-background vectors. All are finite;
+their norms and target-to-bath distances reproduce the JSON statistics.
+
+| Head | Target score | Background mean | Background SD | Target attention | Target value norm | Weighted bath norm | Target–bath distance |
+| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
+| L23.H4 | 23.15 | 6.74 | 4.38 | .702 | 11.37 | 7.69 | 9.70 |
+| L23.H5 | 16.88 | 4.98 | 3.34 | .341 | 11.37 | 5.87 | 9.64 |
+| L23.H30 | 15.34 | 3.68 | 3.31 | .273 | 10.66 | 4.69 | 8.55 |
+| L24.H5 | 18.19 | 4.53 | 3.85 | .342 | 15.07 | 9.38 | 14.35 |
+| L24.H13 | 14.46 | 3.50 | 3.32 | .246 | 11.19 | 6.81 | 9.29 |
+| L24.H20 | 25.28 | 6.44 | 4.95 | .891 | 17.10 | 10.40 | 16.63 |
+| L24.H22 | 37.33 | 9.32 | 7.37 | .971 | 17.10 | 11.28 | 17.49 |
+| L24.H23 | 33.28 | 7.55 | 6.63 | .976 | 17.10 | 10.83 | 16.54 |
+
+Entries average per-query measurements, including the per-query background SD;
+they are not moments of one pooled Gaussian. Background means every causally
+visible key except the current target event, including prompt, table, sink and
+run tokens. Scores are scaled, post-RoPE QK products; values precede output
+projection. The weighted and unweighted background means differ in normed
+distance by 4.55–8.85 across heads. A single Gaussian background assumption and
+an unweighted value bath are therefore not established by these measurements.
+No score-to-accuracy law, asymptotic horizon, or causal mediation claim follows
+from this table. It supplies the measurements missing from the existing records,
+without retroactively changing the registered experiment.
+
+## 6. Intervention outcome
+
+**Unaudited.** All 78 planned tapes were scored, with no missing records, changed
+tapes, replacement draws, refits, or length substitutions. The 256-event smoke
+is excluded. Every first-error record, error count, margin and argmax was checked
+against the downloaded per-token NPZ arrays.
+
+| Regime | Length | Failures / tapes | First read / first state | Frozen predicted failure |
+| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
+| Z | 2,048 | 2 / 16 | 0 / 2 | 0 |
+| Z | 8,192 | 1 / 16 | 0 / 1 | 0 |
+| H | 2,048 | 0 / 11 | 0 / 0 | .1518 |
+| H | 8,192 | 2 / 11 | 0 / 2 | .4795 |
+| F | 2,048 | 12 / 12 | 11 / 1 | .1963 |
+| F | 8,192 | 12 / 12 | 10 / 2 | .1963 |
+
+The collision gaps Δ_C are **−.1250** and **+.1193**. Length gaps Δ_L(Z),
+Δ_L(H), Δ_F are **−.0625, +.1818, 0**. The registered numerical reading is
+**mixed**, independently of H being below its distinct-tape floor. The causal
+test therefore does not pass, and is formally **inconclusive**, not evidence for
+the opposite universal claim that length alone causes failure.
+
+| Frozen model | Prospective mean log score | Collision minus this model |
+| --- | ---: | ---: |
+| Collision | −4.45727 | — |
+| Log dilution | −3.88656 | −.57071 |
+| Inverse-t dilution | −4.40702 | −.05025 |
+| Position-only | −3.85854 | −.59873 |
+| Short-fit lognormal | −4.14613 | −.31114 |
+
+The prospective test **fails against every alternative**. Zero-conflict first
+errors are state errors, so they refute this predictor of *any first run error*,
+not a claim that every read error requires a suffix conflict. There are no first
+read errors in Z or H. Of F's 24 first errors, 21 are reads: **19 at step 2,046**,
+exactly the first new tail symbol, and two earlier on long tapes (992 and 1,075).
+Three are state errors. Thus F's failure rate is saturated at both lengths;
+Δ_F = 0 is not persuasive evidence of length independence. Several pairs change
+first-error timing or kind despite equal conflict counts.
+
+The constructed regimes also change periodicity, symbol frequency and boundary
+novelty, and hold the literal table fixed. They are not random samples from a
+population or a surgical intervention on attention keys. Wilson bars in the
+machine-readable summary and figure are descriptive binomial intervals, not a
+causal confidence guarantee. With one frozen program, few distinct tapes and
+an inconclusive H cell, the evidence supports rejection of this registered
+constant-q model, not a general rejection of content-address interference.
+
+![Held-out calibration and intervention outcomes, unaudited](results/horizon.png)
+
+## 7. Consequence for the paper
+
+Do **not** add a predictive horizon law or "collisions, not decay" conclusion to
+the paper. C2's narrowed contribution has not been achieved. A suitable statement
+for the "where does it fail" section is:
+
+> On Savant r2's trained formats, a preregistered suffix-conflict hazard estimated
+> from early run prefixes beat four short-fit baselines in held-out log score,
+> but substantially overpredicted survival at 8k and 12k events. Constructed
+> tapes did not reproduce the required collision-versus-length contrasts, and
+> the frozen hazard lost to all four baselines prospectively. Sparse, clustered
+> short-context errors did not identify an effective address length or a stable
+> conflict sensitivity. These unaudited results do not support a quantitative
+> collision horizon for this executor.
+
+Boundary-sensitive errors and separate read/state hazards are possible follow-up
+hypotheses, explicitly **post-hoc**, not discoveries established by this test.
+The short-tape score/value measurements are descriptive evidence only. The
+birthday and lognormal calculations remain classical conditional models, as
+GATE §C2 requires. No new theorem, universal mechanism or fitted-curve rescue is
+claimed. No additional spend is needed to report this negative result.
+
+## 8. Artifacts, checks and spend
+
+- Frozen data-only estimates: `results/estimate.json` (unchanged from takeover;
+  recomputation matched SHA-256 `b935a6a78fee5010e9ccf6005f9533e8da478812dab388a011aabaad9f31d858`
+  of canonical sorted-key JSON).
+- Prospective manifest and compact predictions: `results/intervention_manifest.json`
+  and `results/intervention_plan.json`, committed at `40e28ac7` before any GPU forward.
+- Raw outcomes: `results/intervention/records.json` and 78 per-tape NPZ files.
+  Summary: `results/intervention_summary.json`; figure: `results/horizon.{png,svg}`.
+- Supplement: `results/short-stats/short_stats.json` and `short_values.npz`.
+- Budget and call lifecycle: `results/ledger.json`; each job also has `_result.json`.
+
+Validation: 13 CPU tests passed, including brute-force collision equivalence,
+distinct tapes, exact fixed-count pairs, likelihood flooring, and rejecting
+incomplete or duplicate outcome sets. All 78 outcome summaries agree with raw
+per-token arrays; all 480 supplementary score/value observations have finite
+vectors and matching norms. The figure was rendered and visually inspected.
+
+Local analysis can be reproduced without GPU spend:
+
+```sh
+nice -n 19 uv run --no-project --with numpy --with pytest python -m pytest research/horizon/test_hz.py -q
+nice -n 19 uv run --no-project --with numpy python research/horizon/hz_report.py
+nice -n 19 uv run --no-project --with numpy --with matplotlib python research/horizon/hz_plot.py
+```
+
+For a fresh data-only estimation recheck, run `hz_estimate.py` with numpy, scipy,
+tokenizers and huggingface_hub, setting `--out` to a **new** JSON path. It refuses
+to overwrite an existing estimate. The execution-HEAD provenance field changes
+on a later commit; scientific fields should agree. This script reads REGVM
+without writing Python import caches there. Run lengthy local rechecks detached
+with output redirected, as done here. Do not respawn the settled GPU job IDs.
+
+| Job | Modal call | Status | Estimated cost |
+| --- | --- | --- | ---: |
+| Smoke (uncounted) | `fc-01M63A3XBWF4PVJGR8F8M31GK7` | collected, complete | $0.2717 |
+| Intervention | `fc-01M63A5M63NEYFVQ8MS4MKS5A5` | collected, complete | $0.3278 |
+| Short-tape supplement | `fc-01M63A5N1HG3B8QPQJJ220J8BF` | collected, complete | $0.2662 |
+| **Total** | | **no running HORIZON jobs** | **$0.8657 / $15** |
+
+All jobs used NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3; CPU vendor/model metadata is in the ledger.
+Cost includes the conservative per-job startup allowance described above and is
+not an invoice. All code and artifacts are committed only on branch `horizon`;
+nothing is pushed, and no other experiment's jobs or volumes were modified.
